---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const updated = '18 September 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy policy | 88cutouts"
  description="What 88cutouts collects, what it doesn't, and the third-party services involved. No accounts, no sign-up, no personal data collected directly."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="prose">
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">Last updated {updated}.</p>

      <p>
        88cutouts has no accounts and no sign-up. You never give us your name, email
        address or any other personal detail to use the site, and there is no server that
        stores anything you do here. Copying a sticker, setting its opacity, downloading one, and
        typing in the cutout text maker all happen entirely in your own browser.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        We use <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> to understand how many people visit and
        which stickers get used. It sets cookies and records things like the pages you
        view, your approximate location (country/city level, derived from your IP address),
        and your device and browser type. We also record when someone copies or downloads a
        sticker, and what terms are searched for — so we know what to draw next. None of
        this identifies you personally, and we never try to link it to a real identity.
      </p>
      <p>
        Google's own handling of this data is covered by the
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
          Google Privacy Policy</a>. You can opt out across all sites with the
        <a
          href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          target="_blank">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>, or by blocking
        cookies in your browser settings — the site works exactly the same either way.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising</h2>
      <p>
        We intend to show ads through <strong>Google AdSense</strong>. Ads are not running
        yet. When they are, Google and its partners may use cookies to serve ads based on
        your prior visits to this and other websites. You can manage this at
        <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
          Google My Ad Center</a>. This page will be updated when ads go live.
      </p>

      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        The site is served as static files by <strong>Cloudflare Pages</strong>. Cloudflare
        processes standard request logs (including IP addresses) to deliver the site and
        protect it from abuse. Fonts are self-hosted, so no font provider sees your visit.
      </p>

      <h2>What we don't do</h2>
      <p>
        We don't sell data, we don't run email marketing, we don't have a newsletter, and
        we don't ask you to log in. There is no user-generated content, and nothing you type
        into the cutout text maker ever leaves your device — the letters are drawn onto a
        canvas inside your browser and the finished PNG is never uploaded.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        The only cookies set on this site come from the third parties above — Google
        Analytics, and Google AdSense once ads are live. The site itself sets none, and it
        stores nothing in your browser's local storage. Blocking cookies entirely does not
        break anything here: every sticker, the opacity control and the cutout text maker
        all work the same way with cookies switched off.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You can block cookies in your browser settings, use the Google Analytics opt-out
        add-on linked above, or use any content blocker — none of it affects how the site
        works. If you are in the EEA, UK or another region with consent requirements, you
        can also withdraw consent at any time through the same browser settings.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        This site isn't directed at children under 13 and we don't knowingly collect data
        from them.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about any of this, or want something removed? Email
        <a href="mailto:hello@88cutouts.com">hello@88cutouts.com</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
